{
  "note": "Normative expected outcomes of the webhook delivery interop matrix (interop/README.md section 15, interop/webhook/contract.md). `sender` fixes the sender argv the driver builds (`messages`, `allowlist`, `signing_key`, `jack_key`, `subscription_id`, `resolver`, `rebind_address`, `body`, `clock_offset`; fixture names resolve against spec/fixtures/keys.json); `receiver` fixes the receiver argv (`start`, `card`, `enforce`, `require_jack`, `pending_secret`, `mcp_server_kid`, `enqueue_fail`, `clock_offset`); `relay` names the tamper preset or is null for a direct connection; `shadow` binds the loopback alias 127.0.0.2 at the receiver's port; `expected.shadow_connections` fixes how many connections the shadow listener may accept, `0` stating that the policy refusal happened before any dial, and `expected.shadow_bytes` fixes how many bytes it may receive (`0` for DNS rebinding: Go dials and then compares the peer, so a connection is allowed, a TLS handshake or request byte is not); `gap` maps a sender language to the reason its cell is skipped; `cross_check: false` turns off the driver's comparison of the relay's recorded request with the receiver's delivery line, which is needed when the relay rewrites a header after signing. `expected.sender` is matched as a recursive subset against the sender's result line; every relay-bearing scenario states `expected.attempts`, matched positionally against the relay's recorded requests because the sender prints no attempt lines, and an attempt record carries the same `signatures` shape as a delivery, recomputed by the driver from the bytes the relay recorded, so `valid: true` there states that the sender signed the bytes it wrote; `expected.deliveries` positionally against the receiver's delivery lines, whose `enqueued` counts the forwarded messages of the process and whose `forwarded` names the bodies the receiver passed to its durable enqueue. Arrays match with equal length and element-wise subsets. `$sub` and `$url` are the driver's derived subscription id and the sender's callback URL, `$kid:<name>` and `$public_key:<name>` resolve to the fixture kid and public key, and `t0` is 1800000000. Every signature in `signatures` is recomputed by the driver with the pinned delivery secret and the public keys of the scenario's `receiver.card` set, so `valid: false` states that no card key of that scenario verifies the entry.",
  "scenario_order": [
    "deliver-v1",
    "deliver-w1",
    "deliver-asymmetric",
    "refuse-unpublished-signing-key",
    "refuse-jack-server-key",
    "verify-challenge",
    "verify-challenge-w1",
    "refuse-tampered-body",
    "refuse-tampered-header",
    "refuse-stale-timestamp",
    "refuse-future-timestamp",
    "refuse-unknown-subscription",
    "refuse-unknown-envelope-type",
    "refuse-malformed-body",
    "refuse-body-too-large",
    "dedup-repeated-delivery",
    "control-gap",
    "control-terminated",
    "retry-http-503",
    "retry-enqueue-failed",
    "ssrf-private-address",
    "ssrf-dns-rebinding"
  ],
  "scenarios": {
    "deliver-v1": {
